.TH WIFICAPC 8 "2026" "WiFiCapC" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
wificapc \- native 802.11 monitor-mode capture daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wificapc
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wificapc
is a small, passive 802.11 capture daemon for Linux (built for the
Raspberry Pi Zero 2 W's 2.4 GHz brcmfmac radio). It puts an interface into
monitor mode, hops channels, builds AP/STA recon tables, collects WPA
4-way handshakes and PMKIDs into per-pair
.B .pcap
and hashcat
.B .22000
files, and can inject association and deauthentication frames.
.PP
The daemon is deliberately
.BR passive :
it performs no policy of its own beyond optional autonomous attacks. A
client (for example the pwnagotchi agent) drives it over a Unix-socket
JSON protocol \(em see
.BR "PROTOCOL" .
.SH OPTIONS
.SS General
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Read options from a
.I key = value
config file before applying command-line flags (so the CLI overrides the
file). Keys mirror the long option names with dashes as underscores:
.BR socket ", " mode ", " foreground ", " debug ", " iface ", " hs_dir ", "
.BR channels ", " hop_interval ", " attack ", " attack_interval ", "
.BR mac_rand ", " pmkid_only ", " state_file ", " state_max_age ", "
.BR log_format .
Blank lines and
.B #
comments are ignored.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-socket " " \fIPATH\fR
Unix socket path (default
.BR /run/wificapc.sock ).
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " " \fIOCTAL\fR
Socket file mode (default
.BR 0660 ).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-foreground
Stay in the foreground and log to stderr.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Enable debug logging.
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-format " " \fIFMT\fR
Log output format when not using syslog:
.B text
(default) or
.BR json
(one JSON object per line, for structured log ingestion).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SS Auto-start
If
.B \-\-iface
is given the daemon brings the radio up and starts capturing immediately,
without waiting for a client.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-iface " " \fIIFACE\fR
Wireless interface to use (e.g.
.BR wlan0 ).
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-hs\-dir " " \fIPATH\fR
Handshake output directory (default
.BR /etc/pwnagotchi/handshakes ).
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-channels " " \fILIST\fR
Comma-separated channels to hop (default 1\-13).
.TP
.BR \-\-hop\-interval " " \fIMS\fR
Per-channel dwell time in milliseconds (default 250).
.SS Autonomous standalone mode
.TP
.B \-\-auto
Self-driving mode: create a monitor vif on the base interface's radio
(given by
.BR \-i ,
default
.BR wlan0 ),
auto-detect the regdomain's channels, hop them while sniffing, attack each
channel's APs on the dwell (PMKID-first directed association, deauth
associated clients to force the 4-way), and write
.B .pcap
/
.B .22000
artifacts — all with no external driver. The radio must present monitor
support; on brcmfmac the driver reload needed to expose it is the
environment's responsibility (the image's prep/launcher), not this daemon's.
If a monitor vif already exists it is reused.
.SS Autonomous attacks
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-attack
Enable autonomous deauth+assoc attacks against visible targets.
.TP
.BR \-\-attack\-interval " " \fIMS\fR
Attack scheduling period in milliseconds (default 5000).
.TP
.B \-\-mac\-rand
Use a fresh locally-administered, unicast random MAC for every
association frame.
.TP
.B \-\-pmkid\-only
Autonomous attack sends association frames only (PMKID elicitation) and
never deauthenticates clients: quieter and faster target cycling.
.SS Recon persistence
.TP
.BR \-\-state\-file " " \fIPATH\fR
File the AP/STA recon tables are dumped to on shutdown and reloaded from on
start (default
.BR /tmp/wificapc/state.bin ).
Pass an empty string to disable.
.TP
.BR \-\-state\-max\-age " " \fIS\fR
Ignore persisted recon state older than
.I S
seconds (default 600).
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.BR SIGINT ", " SIGTERM
Shut down cleanly: close the capture socket, return the interface to
managed mode, and persist the recon table.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exits non-zero on a fatal error. In particular, exit code
.B 3
is used by the rx-silence capture-health watchdog to signal a wedged radio
so that
.BR systemd (1)
restarts the service and re-initialises the driver.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /run/wificapc.sock
Default control socket.
.TP
.B /etc/pwnagotchi/handshakes/
Default handshake output directory.
.TP
.B /tmp/wificapc/state.bin
Default persisted recon table.
.SH PROTOCOL
The line-delimited JSON command/event protocol is documented in
.IR docs/protocol.md
in the source distribution.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR iw (8),
.BR hashcat (1)
.SH AUTHORS
Asif Iqbal Gazi and contributors.
